---
layout: base.njk
title: Help
description: How to use Prospektor Studio — guides, answers and a search box, served straight from the running product so they always describe the version that is live.
faqs:
  - q: What does Prospektor cost?
    a: $999 a month per workspace, taken by Stripe. The scan on the home page is free and needs no sign-up — point it at a site and it reads that company before it says a word about them.
  - q: Do I have to install anything?
    a: No. Prospektor Studio runs in the browser at studio.prospektor.ai. There is nothing to download and no extension to add.
  - q: Can I run Prospektor for my clients?
    a: Yes. An agency-flagged workspace gets New client workspace in the workspace switcher, for the agency's owner or admins — name the client and a researched workspace exists before the next screen. A portfolio upload creates a whole roster at once. Each client workspace is billed as its own workspace.
    link: /help/#guide-workspace
    linkLabel: Read the workspace guide
  - q: Who at my company can sign in?
    a: If you bought with a company address, the access list carries your whole domain as well as your own address, so everyone at that company can sign in — including addresses that do not exist yet. An owner can keep that or narrow it to named addresses.
    link: /help/#guide-workspace
    linkLabel: Members and access
  - q: What happens if I stop paying?
    a: The workspace pauses rather than disappears. The lock screen's resubscribe button reopens the same studio with everything kept. Deleting a workspace is a separate, deliberate act in the danger zone, only an owner may do it, and it cannot be undone.
  - q: What do you do with my data?
    a: The privacy page is the full answer, and it is written to be read rather than to be survived. In short - the studio holds no card details, sets only the cookies that sign you in, and makes no third-party requests.
    link: /privacy/
    linkLabel: Read the privacy page
---

<header class="help-hero">
  <div class="help-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">help</span>
    <h1 class="help-h1">How can we help?</h1>
    <p class="help-lede">Guides and step-by-step answers for Prospektor Studio. This page reads the same documentation the product itself runs on, so it always describes the version that is live.</p>
    <div class="help-search">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M11 11l3.2 3.2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      <input id="helpSearch" type="search" placeholder="Search the guides — try &ldquo;how do I create a new workspace&rdquo;" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Search the help guides">
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

{#- The search results take the page over while a query is live: the cards and
    the guides below are both hidden, and this is the only panel on screen. -#}
<section id="helpResults" class="help-results" aria-live="polite" hidden></section>

{#- ── the hub: a card per guide ──
    Cards are built at build time from the corpus (#136) and rebuilt by help.js
    only if the live corpus has actually moved since — see the hash on
    #helpGuides. The grid is the one #144 shipped for /resources/; the CSS is
    shared rather than copied. -#}
<section id="helpHub" class="help-hub">
  {%- if help.guides.length %}
  <ul class="card-grid">
    {%- for g in help.guides %}
    <li class="card">
      <a href="#guide-{{ g.slug }}">
        <span class="card-emoji" aria-hidden="true">{{ g.emoji }}</span>
        <span class="card-topic">{{ g.topic }}</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">{{ g.title }}</h2>
        <p class="card-dek">{{ g.dek }}</p>
        <span class="card-cta">Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
      </a>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- else %}
  {#- The corpus could not be reached at build time. The page still ships and
      help.js fills this in from the live studio — see src/_data/help.js. -#}
  <p class="help-dim" id="helpHubEmpty">Loading the guides…</p>
  {%- endif %}
</section>

{#- ── the guides themselves ──
    Every guide, in the served HTML. This is #136: before this, a crawler was
    handed the word "Loading…" and ten guides of long-tail content were
    invisible. `data-corpus-hash` is what stops the browser re-rendering all of
    this a second time for nothing. -#}
<section id="helpGuides" class="help-guides" data-corpus-hash="{{ help.hash }}" data-corpus-source="{{ help.source }}">
  {%- for g in help.guides %}
  <article class="help-guide" id="guide-{{ g.slug }}" data-slug="{{ g.slug }}">
    <span class="help-guide-topic">{{ g.emoji }} {{ g.topic }}</span>
    {{ g.html | safe }}
    <a class="help-guide-top" href="#helpHub">↑ All guides</a>
  </article>
  {%- endfor %}
</section>

<section class="help-faq">
  <div class="help-faq-inner">
    <h2 class="help-faq-h2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <dl class="help-faq-list">
      {%- for item in faqs %}
      <div class="help-faq-item">
        <dt>{{ item.q }}</dt>
        <dd>{{ item.a }}{% if item.link %} <a href="{{ item.link }}">{{ item.linkLabel }} →</a>{% endif %}</dd>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="help-support">
  <div class="help-support-inner">
    <span class="tag">still stuck</span>
    <h2>Ask a person.</h2>
    <p>The <strong>Support</strong> pill inside the studio answers in seconds and already knows which workspace you are in. If you would rather write, we read every mail.</p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
    <p class="help-support-alt"><a href="https://studio.prospektor.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the studio ↗</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The visible FAQ above and this are rendered from the same frontmatter list,
    so the structured data cannot drift from what the page says. -#}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for item in faqs %}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ item.q | dump | safe }},
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | dump | safe }} }
    }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

{#- The corpus the build rendered from, verbatim, for help.js: it is what the
    search index is built from before any network call, and what the live
    corpus is compared against so the page is not re-rendered for nothing. -#}
<script type="application/json" id="helpCorpus">{{ help.corpusJson | safe }}</script>

<script src="/assets/js/help-render.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/help.js"></script>
